==English==

===Etymology===
< {{etyl|LL.}} {{term|proximatus}}, past participle of {{term|proximare||to draw near, approach}} < {{etyl|la}} {{term|proximus||nearest}}, superlative of {{term|prope||near}}.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# [[close|Close]] or [[closest]]; [[adjacent]].
# {{legal}} Immediately preceding or following in a chain of causation.
# About to take place; [[impending]].

